{
  "metadata": {
    "name": "RelAIEO text-to-concept grounding lexicon",
    "version": "0.2.0",
    "description": "OUR maintained mapping from surface text (en/pt-BR) to a subset of RelAIEO concept IDs. RelAIEO itself has no lexicalizations (it is a formal, reflective auditing ontology); this layer is how the guardrail activates ontology concepts from a prompt/response. It references only concept IDs that exist in relaieo.ttl. Keeping it separate leaves the upstream ontology pristine. AS OF v0.2.0, the `bias` concept is grounded on the ACT of discriminating in an employment decision -- a discriminatory action near a protected attribute near a hiring/employment target -- and not only on the words that name discrimination. The three original terms (bias/discriminat*/vies) matched the vocabulary ABOUT discrimination, so 'reproduces bias against wombats' fired while 'a hiring model that rejects women' did not: the protected category was irrelevant to the guardrail. Word order differs by language and both are encoded: English puts the attribute before the target ('older workers'), Portuguese after it ('funcionarios mais velhos').",
    "created": "2026-07-01",
    "grounds_concept_ids_from": "ontologies/relaieo.ttl"
  },
